{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1360776-v20-krainas-ways-rituals","id":1360776,"title":"[V20] Krainas, Ways, Rituals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-13T15:49:25-08:00","id":1360776,"title":"[V20] Krainas, Ways, Rituals","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am confused about Krainas (<i>Enoch, Well</i>) and Ways (<i>Earth, Fire, Air, Water, Spirit, Sorrows</i>) for Koldunic Sorcery, I must choose a Way when starting the discipline, when do the Krainas play a role? Are those alternative Ways?<br /> <br /> Another questions, are Koldunic Sorcerers able to learn all the rituals of Thaumaturgy? The text of the Way of Sorrows seems to imply that they can use the Scry ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T17:03:55-08:00","id":1360787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1360776-v20-krainas-ways-rituals#post1360776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am confused about Krainas (<i>Enoch, Well</i>) and Ways (<i>Earth, Fire, Air, Water, Spirit, Sorrows</i>) for Koldunic Sorcery, I must choose a Way when starting the discipline, when do the Krainas play a role? Are those alternative Ways?<br /> <br /> Another questions, are Koldunic Sorcerers able to learn all the rituals of Thaumaturgy? The text of the Way of Sorrows seems to imply that they can use the Scry ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Krainas are the Old style of kolunic sorcery(previous the anarch-revolt) as outlined in VTM: Dark ages and Tome of Secrets. They're something that you shouldn't find outside of Old Clan Tzimisce and Sabbat kolduns should stick to Ways.<br /> <br /> Old Kolduns(that use Krainas) don't have rituals in the traditional sense as far as I'm aware, they have &quot;Rites&quot;(outlined in VTMDA: Tome of Secrets) which are kind of like the vampiric version of garou gifts.<br /> <br /> Modern Kolduns(that use Ways) can learn thaum rituals. Their discipline is also closer to blood magic than the more spiritual magic of Old Kolduns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T10:34:34-08:00","id":1362451,"title":"","content":"Effectively, they're two different disciplines, old-form Koldunism and new-form Koldunism. Old-form Koldunism is the kraina stuff, and that died out for the most part during the Anarch Revolt. New-form Koldunism are the ways. The only vampires that would realistically be using kraina in a modern nights setting are methuselahs, and in the dark ages setting ways hadn't been invented yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T13:51:31-08:00","id":1362720,"title":"","content":"There's also the implication that while the Kraina were a form of animistic power, tied to all manner of natural spirits, the Ways come specifically from Kupala, a demon (for whatever value of &quot;demon&quot; it is, because that word is broad and nebulous in WoD, because it was broad and nebulous in Real Life).<br /> <br /> From a certain perspective, Way-based Koldunism is practically Infernalism, though Sabbat Kolduns will naturally take exception to that claim, to put it mildly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T05:55:40-07:00","id":1517756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1360776-v20-krainas-ways-rituals?p=1362720#post1362720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the implication that while the Kraina were a form of animistic power, tied to all manner of natural spirits, the Ways come specifically from Kupala, a demon (for whatever value of &quot;demon&quot; it is, because that word is broad and nebulous in WoD, because it was broad and nebulous in Real Life).<br /> <br /> From a certain perspective, Way-based Koldunism is practically Infernalism, though Sabbat Kolduns will naturally take exception to that claim, to put it mildly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to ask where this is implied. Which book was this particular difference in nature established?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28096-vlad_tepes","name":"Vlad_Tepes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28096_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T21:27:50-07:00","id":1517859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vlad_Tepes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1360776-v20-krainas-ways-rituals?p=1517756#post1517756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to ask where this is implied. Which book was this particular difference in nature established?</div> </div> </div> </div>The books have gone back and forth about whether Koldunism has always been inherently &quot;demonic&quot;, or if it was corrupted by Kupala. As V20/DAV20 went on, it sort of leaned toward the latter. With its differentiation between Ways and Kraina.<br /> <br /> Black Hand V20 however made this idea more explicit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20 - The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra, p. 169</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In ancient times, the vows of this wedding were expressed through the kraina (the sorcerous Path) that would arise and mature with the Tzimisce who cultivated koldunism. In those ancient days, the Genius Loci was a tool attainable by all koldun to enhance their kraina... The chaos that beset the Clan during the formation of the Sabbat made entrance for the demon Kupala to entreat promises of tremendous might to those desperate enough to listen. And many did, soliciting the demon for assistance to defeat their enemies.<br /> By defiling the Genius Loci (known to the modern koldun as the Way of the Spirit), the demon spread its primal, dark, elemental, and depraved sorcery throughout the Clan to any who agreed to divorce themselves from their ancient kraina, trading their godhood to bow and pledge themselves in veneration to the new demon-god.</div> </div> </div> </div>See also DAV20: Tome of Secrets, where a Tzimisce speaker in the Dark Ages describes, with horror and dismay, that their Clan is slowly becoming corrupted by Kupala's influence.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}